De-duplicate libraries on link lines where the linker does not need repeats.

Applies to picoquic 70b5fd5aafdd2d6c349ff783202ece9d778bcaf2, after 0001.

picoquic's targets list the same static archives more than once, and Apple's
linker warns about each repeat. CMake 3.29 and later (policy CMP0156, set NEW when available) drop repeats
for linkers that do not need them and keep them for linkers that do.
Tests: adapters/picoquic's source-mode link policy check
(picoquic_source_mode_link_policy).

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index a7d2c346..37456ec2 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,10 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.13)
+# De-duplicate libraries on link lines when the linker does not need the
+# repeats (CMake 3.29 and later). Apple's linker warns about repeated static
+# libraries; linkers that need repeats keep them.
+if(POLICY CMP0156)
+    cmake_policy(SET CMP0156 NEW)
+endif()
 
 # Building tests by default depends on whether this is a subproject
 if(DEFINED PROJECT_NAME)
